# Environment and Configuration

## Environment Variables

```bash
# All optional — the app runs with nothing set.
export LEMONADE_URL="http://localhost:13305/api/v1"  # Explicit external server instead of the owned runtime
export LEMONADE_API_KEY="..."                        # Optional inference key override
export LEMONADE_ADMIN_API_KEY="..."                  # Optional management key override
export UFORGE_SCHEMA_DIR="./defaults/schemas/Sine Nomine"  # load_default_schemas() override
export RUST_LOG=info                                 # Log verbosity

export UFORGE_SKIP_EMBEDDED_LEMONADE=1   # Skip automatic runtime provisioning
export UFORGE_LEMOND_PATH="/path/to/lemonade/lemond" # Owned-development binary override
```

The desktop application has one canonical user profile:

- `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/u-forge/u-forge.toml` (fallback: `~/.config/u-forge/u-forge.toml`)
- `$XDG_DATA_HOME/u-forge` (fallback: `~/.local/share/u-forge`) for databases and editable seeded defaults
- `$XDG_CACHE_HOME/u-forge/lemonade` (fallback: `~/.cache/u-forge/lemonade`) for expendable Lemonade state

The current working directory is never searched for `u-forge.toml`. At first
launch, the packaged config template is transformed to absolute XDG data paths,
and packaged schemas/example data are copied into the data directory. A defaults
revision marker makes that seed one-time: user edits and deletions are not
restored implicitly. A later defaults revision requires an explicit migration.

### Module-specific logging

```bash
export RUST_LOG=u_forge_core::graph::storage=debug,u_forge_core::ai::embeddings=info

# Lemonade discovery plus redacted stdout/stderr from the owned lemond child.
export RUST_LOG=info,u_forge_core::lemonade::management=debug,u_forge_core::lemonade::embedded::lemond=debug
```

`RUST_LOG` controls u-forge's tracing filter. Embeddable Lemonade has its own
`log_level` setting in `$XDG_CACHE_HOME/u-forge/lemonade/config.json`, or
`~/.cache/u-forge/lemonade/config.json` when `XDG_CACHE_HOME` is unset. Models
and downloaded backends live under that same cache root; model paths never
fall back to the global Hugging Face cache.
The typed `[lemonade].max_loaded_models` u-forge setting defaults to `1` and is
applied idempotently to the app-owned server through `POST /internal/set` before
provider activation. Lemonade interprets this as a per-model-type residency
limit. External servers are operator-owned and are never changed implicitly.
Set that JSON field to `"debug"` when Lemonade's default informational child
events are insufficient; u-forge forwards those lines only when the dedicated
`lemond` tracing target above is enabled and redacts both runtime credentials.

## Import Path Resolution

The desktop app reads `[data].schema_dir` and `[data].import_file` from its XDG
configuration to pre-populate the new-world flow and explicit import dialogs.
The lower-level
`SchemaIngestion::load_default_schemas()` helper checks `UFORGE_SCHEMA_DIR`
and otherwise uses `./defaults/schemas`. It does not descend into subdirectories;
select the schema set directory itself, such as `defaults/schemas/Sine Nomine`.

## Database Location

`KnowledgeGraph::new(db_path)` opens (or creates) a SQLite database at
`<db_path>/knowledge.db`. The directory is created automatically.

`[storage].embedding_dimensions` and
`[storage].high_quality_embedding_dimensions` configure the two sqlite-vec
lanes (defaults: 768 and 4096). Dimensions are persisted in database metadata;
changing either value requires rebuilding the database.

The desktop app uses the persistent path from `[storage].db_path`.

