## Lemonade Server

Lemonade Server provides all AI inference (embedding, reranking, chat, STT,
TTS) via an OpenAI-compatible HTTP API. On x86_64 Linux with GNU libc, building
the desktop UI downloads the checksum-pinned upstream Ubuntu x64 Embeddable
[Lemonade 2026.48.3 release](https://github.com/lemonade-sdk/lemonade/releases/tag/v2026.48.3)
into `target/`. `make release` packages that runtime, the desktop executable,
and the complete defaults tree into an AppImage built on Ubuntu 26.04. The
build adds the `reasoning` catalog label to built-in Gemma 4 GGUF models and
retains the upstream backend version manifest. If provisioning is skipped or
unavailable, AI features degrade gracefully and the knowledge graph remains
usable.

### Standalone setup and upgrade notes

Use the [upstream installers](https://github.com/lemonade-sdk/lemonade/releases)
for an external server. Use `lemonade backends` to inspect available runtimes,
`lemonade pull <model>` to download a model, and `GET /v1/health` to check the
server and its loaded models. Install FLM with `lemonade backends install flm:npu`
on supported hardware before selecting its dynamically discovered models.

- Owned launches retain their existing private cache and config in Lemonade's
  portable mode. A fresh install writes only u-forge's config overrides.
  Upgrading an external system service is separate; see the
  [upstream migration guide](https://github.com/lemonade-sdk/lemonade/wiki/Migration#v117x--v1180---v1181).
- [Lemonade 11.8.0](https://github.com/lemonade-sdk/lemonade/releases/tag/v11.8.0)
  made Whisper auto-detect the input language when none is supplied, and changed
  explicit `llamacpp_args` to replace model and architecture arguments.
- The first ROCm model load may download the new
  [ROCm 10 runtime](https://github.com/lemonade-sdk/lemonade/releases/tag/v2026.41.1).
- For an authenticated external server, supply its inference key in
  `LEMONADE_API_KEY`. An empty admin key no longer bypasses authentication as of
  [2026.47.1](https://github.com/lemonade-sdk/lemonade/releases/tag/v2026.47.1).

### Lemonade connection selection

The desktop uses `lemonade::resolve_runtime_connection()` at startup:
`LEMONADE_URL` selects an external connection, otherwise the app launches its
private pinned runtime on an available loopback port. It must not adopt a
process already listening on a candidate port. If the selected connection is
unavailable, graph functionality still works.

`lemonade::resolve_lemonade_url()` is for external-server discovery, including
direct Cargo integration tests. It normalizes `LEMONADE_URL` without a health
probe when set; otherwise it probes `/v1/health` on `localhost:13305` and then
`127.0.0.1:13305` (2 s timeout per request). Keep that probe out of desktop
startup and the [canonical test fixture](testing-debugging.mdc#canonical-suites).

### Endpoints in Use

| Endpoint | Method | Provider / Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `/api/v1/models` | GET | `LemonadeServerCatalog::discover()` |
| `/system-info` | GET | `LemonadeServerCatalog::discover()` — installed backends |
| `/api/v1/health` | GET | `LemonadeServerCatalog::discover()` + manual verification |
| `/api/v1/load` | POST | `load_model()` — load a model before inference |
| `/api/v1/embeddings` | POST (JSON) | `LemonadeProvider` |
| `/api/v1/audio/transcriptions` | POST (multipart) | `LemonadeTranscriptionProvider` (no GPU lock) / `LemonadeSttProvider` (GPU-managed) |
| `/api/v1/audio/speech` | POST (JSON) | `LemonadeTtsProvider` |
| `/api/v1/chat/completions` | POST (JSON) | `LemonadeChatProvider` |
| `/api/v1/rerank` | POST (JSON) | `LemonadeRerankProvider` |

## Troubleshooting

| Problem | Fix |
|---|---|
| `Lemonade Server not available` | Check the owned runtime; if using a standalone server, verify the desktop's `LEMONADE_URL` |
| `lemonade pull` fails | Check disk space, network access, and whether the model's backend is installed |
| Schema not found | Verify the selected schema directory directly contains the schema JSON files; desktop paths come from `[data].schema_dir`, not `UFORGE_SCHEMA_DIR` |
| Dimension mismatch | Ensure each embedding model matches its configured vector lane; rebuild the database after changing dimensions |
| Whisper not loaded in RAM | First transcription call triggers load; subsequent calls are fast. `GET /api/v1/health` shows loaded models |
| Transcription error: "Could not open audio data" | Audio bytes empty or not a valid WAV/MP3/OGG |
